Capstone Data Import Guide

You are working with the full DataCo Global Logistics dataset (180,000+ rows). Because of this scale, you cannot simply copy-paste data. You must use the PostgreSQL command-line utility to ingest the raw file.

Step 1: Prepare the Environment

Ensure DataCoSupplyChainDataset.csv is in your Unit_16_Capstone/data directory.

Step 2: Initialize Staging

Run Setup_Staging.sql to create the raw_staging table. This table is a flat, unnormalized container designed to hold the raw CSV import before you transform it into your 3NF schema.

Step 3: Execute the Bulk Import

Open your terminal and ensure you are in the project root. Run this command:

psql -U postgres -d cosc2409 -c "\copy raw_staging FROM 'Unit_16_Capstone/data/DataCoSupplyChainDataset.csv' WITH CSV HEADER;"


Note: If you see COPY 180519, the ingestion was successful.

Performance Tip: If the import takes more than a few seconds, it is normal. You are moving roughly 15MB of structured data.

Step 4: Verification

Once the data is ingested, perform a quick check to ensure the rows exist before you start your INSERT INTO ... SELECT DISTINCT migrations:

SELECT count(*) FROM raw_staging;


You are now ready to write your init_schema.sql and normalize the data.
